{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "היום הזה ה' אלהיך מצוך לעשות", :translit "ha-yom ha-zeh Hashem Elokekha metzavkha la'asot", :gloss "this day YHWH your Elohim commands you to do"} {:he "ויתן להם ארצות גוים", :translit "va-yiten lahem artzot goyim", :gloss "and He gave them lands of nations"} {:he "בעבור ישמרו חקיו ותורותיו ינצורו", :translit "ba'avur yishmeru chukav u'torotav yintzoru", :gloss "that they might keep His statutes and His laws they should observe"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verbal link: מצוך (commands you) echoes ינצורו (observe/guard) of Psalm 105:44-45"}], :frame {:text "Psalm 105:44-45 states that God gave Israel lands of nations so that they would keep His statutes and observe His laws. The Ba'al HaTurim reads this verse as an explication of the purpose behind the commandments given 'this day' in Deuteronomy 26:16.", :sources ["Psalms 105:44-45" "Deuteronomy 26:16"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בכל לבבך ובכל נפשך", :translit "b'chol l'vavkha u'v'chol nafsh'kha", :gloss "with all your heart and with all your soul"} {:he "את ה' האמרת", :translit "et Hashem he'emarta", :gloss "YHWH you have declared"} {:he "בכל לבבך ובכל נפשך", :translit "b'chol l'vavkha u'v'chol nafsh'kha", :gloss "with all your heart and with all your soul"} {:he "אתם עשיתוני חטיבה אחת בארץ", :translit "atem asitemoni chativah achat ba'aretz", :gloss "you have made me one band in the land"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'with all your heart and with all your soul' is immediately followed by 'You have declared YHWH,' linking the two"} {:kind :other, :note "Equation: 'with all your heart and with all your soul' = the Shema, since the identical phrase appears in Deuteronomy 6:5"}], :frame {:text "Deuteronomy 6:5 commands love of God 'with all your heart and with all your soul,' the central phrase of the Shema. The same phrase appears in Deuteronomy 26:16, and its juxtaposition with 'You have declared YHWH' (Deuteronomy 26:17) links the acceptance of God's sovereignty there to the Shema. The phrase 'You have made me one band in the land' is attributed to Israel (Berakhot 6a), expressing that the Shema unifies the Jewish people in their declaration of God's oneness.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 6:5" "Deuteronomy 26:16-17" "Berakhot 6a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verbal link: מצוך (commands you) echoes ינצורו (observe/guard) of Psalm 105:44-45", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'with all your heart and with all your soul' is immediately followed by 'You have declared YHWH,' linking the two", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Equation: 'with all your heart and with all your soul' = the Shema, since the identical phrase appears in Deuteronomy 6:5", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:40.206244347Z", :model "glm-5.2"}